---
import SiteFrame from "../layouts/SiteFrame.astro";
const updated = "August 30, 2026";
---
<SiteFrame title="Terms — Blaine County Preparedness"
           description="How The Table works, and what's expected of everyone at it.">
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
    <h1 class="h1">How we sit at this table</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <p class="lede">
      This is a neighbors' site. The rules are short because most of them
      come down to not being the reason we need more rules.
    </p>

    <h2>Using the site</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone can read. To post, you sign in with a Google account. You're
      responsible for what's posted from your account, so don't hand it
      around.
    </p>

    <h2>What you write</h2>
    <p>
      What you post stays yours. By posting it here you're giving us
      permission to show it on the site — nothing more. We don't claim
      ownership and we won't sell it or license it to anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>What doesn't belong here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Harassment, threats, or targeting people</li>
      <li>Hate directed at anyone for who they are</li>
      <li>Spam, scams, or advertising you weren't invited to post</li>
      <li>Other people's private information</li>
      <li>Anything illegal, or instructions for doing harm</li>
      <li>Impersonating someone else</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Disagreement is welcome and expected — a preparedness forum where
      everyone agrees isn't much use. Contempt is not the same as
      disagreement.
    </p>

    <h2>Moderation</h2>
    <p>
      We can remove any post and block any account. We try to be light-handed
      and we'd rather talk to someone than remove them. New accounts may have
      their first post held briefly for review; this is about spam, not about
      you.
    </p>
    <p>
      If something needs attention, tell us. We'd rather hear from you than
      find it a week later.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site isn't</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing here is professional advice — not medical, legal, engineering,
      or emergency guidance. In a genuine emergency, call the people whose
      job that is. Preparedness discussion is people sharing what they know,
      which is valuable and is not the same as expertise.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do our best to keep the site accurate and available, but we can't
      guarantee either. Use your own judgment about anything you read here.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
      You can leave whenever you want and ask us to delete your account and
      posts. We can close an account that's breaking these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If these terms change meaningfully, we'll say so on the site rather
      than quietly editing the page.
    </p>

    <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, reports, or anything else:
      <a href="mailto:contacts@bcp.zone">contacts@bcp.zone</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="tail">
      See also our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteFrame>

<style>
  .doc { max-width: 66ch; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sage); margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .h1 {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.2rem); line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem; color: var(--snowmelt);
  }
  .updated {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--sage); opacity: 0.7;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--body); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.6; color: var(--sage); margin: 0 0 2.4rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--snowmelt); margin: 2.2rem 0 0.7rem;
  }
  p, li {
    font-family: var(--body); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--snowmelt);
  }
  p { margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  ul { margin: 0 0 1.2rem; padding-left: 1.4rem; }
  li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  a { color: var(--oxide); text-decoration: underline; }
  .tail { margin-top: 2rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--sage); }
</style>
